      "status": "affected",
      "action_statement": "Update nodejs-22 to 22.23.4-0 or later.",
      "status_notes": "CVE-2026-105482 is a Node.js DNS flaw: dns.resolve*() and dns.reverse() silently truncate a hostname at a NUL byte, an incomplete fix of CVE-2026-48930. Node.js fixed it for 22.x in 22.23.4, the 2026-10-21 security release (https://nodejs.org/en/blog/vulnerability/october-2026-security-releases), with commit 19c5056002, 'dns: validate resolve inputs for null bytes' (https://github.com/nodejs/node/commit/19c5056002), which carries this CVE id. Release notes: https://nodejs.org/en/blog/release/v22.23.4. We read the node binary in every published DHI nodejs-22 package for Debian 13 on amd64 and arm64: 22.23.4-0 is the first that reports Node.js v22.23.4; 22.22.3-0 through 22.23.3-0 report Node.js 22.22.3 through 22.23.3."
    },
